Ormeq
=====

Ormeq is a fork of FrogComposband, which descends from Angband by way of
ZAngband, Hengband, Chengband, PosChengband and ComPosband. It inherits its
licensing from that line, and that inheritance is a hard constraint rather
than a choice.

**This software may not be sold.** See "The Angband licence" below.

**The artwork and optional audio ship on narrower terms than the code.**
See "Artwork" and "Sound effects and music".

The full text of every licence named here is in the `licenses/` directory,
which travels with every release.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The game's own source
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

In the inherited tree,
67 of the C source files in `src/` carry this notice -- 65 of them
and nothing else -- and it governs the work as a whole:

    Copyright (c) 1997 Ben Harrison, James E. Wilson, Robert A. Koeneke

    This software may be copied and distributed for educational, research,
    and not for profit purposes provided that this copyright and statement
    are included in all such copies. Other copyrights may also apply.

Angband itself relicensed to GNU GPL v2 in 2009. **This lineage branched
before that and never followed**, so the notice above is the binding one and
the not-for-profit clause stands.

Copyright in the material added since the fork (23 August 2026) is held by
John Horton, and is offered on the same terms.

Full text: `licenses/Angband.txt`

### Inherited dual-licensed files

`src/randname.c` (Antony Sidwell, Sheldon Simms, 2007) and `src/main-cocoa.m`
(Peter Ammon, 2011) are each offered under **either** GNU GPL v2 **or** the
Angband licence. This distribution relies on the Angband branch, which is what
the rest of the tree is under. The unsupported Cocoa frontend is omitted from
public exports, which contain 66 of the notice-bearing files (65 Angband-only).
The GPL text is included for anyone who prefers the other branch.

Full text: `licenses/GPL-2.0.txt`

### Microsoft sample code

`src/readdib.c`, used only by the legacy Win32 frontend, carries Microsoft's
1993 royalty-free sample-code grant. Its notice is retained. Ormeq's small
interface in `src/win_bitmap.h` is supplied under the game's source terms.
The old header and bitmap wall resource are no longer distributed.

Full text: `licenses/Microsoft-Sample-Code.txt`


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Libraries shipped with the game
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

`SDL3.dll`, `SDL3_ttf.dll` and `SDL3_image.dll` are distributed under the
zlib licence.

    Copyright (C) 1997-2026 Sam Lantinga <slouken@libsdl.org>   (SDL3, SDL3_image)
    Copyright (C) 1997-2025 Sam Lantinga <slouken@libsdl.org>   (SDL3_ttf)

Full text: `licenses/SDL3.txt`, `licenses/SDL3_ttf.txt`,
`licenses/SDL3_image.txt`

The DLLs also contain third-party components. Their additional notices are
listed in `licenses/README.md`, with exact source references and DLL hashes
in `licenses/dependency-sources.json`.

SDL3_ttf uses FreeType 2.13.2 and HarfBuzz 8.5.0, already linked into its DLL.
Ormeq distributes FreeType under the FreeType License (FTL), not its GPL
alternative. Portions of this software are copyright (c) 1996-2023 The FreeType
Project (www.freetype.org). All rights reserved.

The image library uses its built-in stb decoder for Ormeq's PNGs; optional
AVIF, TIFF, WebP and libpng DLLs are not bundled. Their names in a DLL string
scan are not evidence that those libraries are embedded. Additional notices
cover the compiled stb, NanoSVG and QOI code.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Fonts shipped with the game
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Five typefaces are bundled in `font/`. Four are under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1 and one under the MIT licence. **Neither licence is satisfied by
a link**; both require their text to travel with the font, which is why it
does.

| font | copyright | licence |
|---|---|---|
| Cozette | (c) 2020-2025 Ines <ines@moonwit.ch> | MIT |
| IBM Plex Mono | Copyright 2017 IBM Corp. | OFL-1.1 |
| Roboto Mono | Copyright 2015 The Roboto Mono Project Authors | OFL-1.1 |
| Share Tech Mono | (c) 2012 Carrois Type Design, Ralph du Carrois, with Reserved Font Name 'Share' | OFL-1.1 |
| VT323 | Copyright 2011 The VT323 Project Authors | OFL-1.1 |

Share Tech Mono carries a **Reserved Font Name**. A modified version of it may
not be distributed under the name "Share". None of these fonts is modified
here; they are shipped as delivered.

Full text: `licenses/OFL-1.1.txt`, `licenses/MIT-Cozette.txt`,
`licenses/fonts.txt`


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Artwork
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

**The artwork is not covered by the licence above, and is licensed to you
separately and more narrowly.**

This applies to:

  * `lib/art/` — the character-art plates (`.art`)
  * `lib/tiles/` — the sprite sheets, terrain atlases and their indexes
  * `_art-src/` — the source images the plates were made from, which are
    kept separately and are not part of the source distribution
  * `_art-held/` — source images held out of the active collection

The artwork belongs to the copyright holder identified in the source section
above and was made for this game. The assets are not derived from Angband or
from anything in the lineage, so the Angband licence does not reach them and
does not grant you anything in respect of them.

You may:

  * **Play the game.** Use the artwork by running Ormeq, for as long as you
    like.
  * **Pass the game on.** Redistribute the complete, unmodified release
    package containing the artwork, free of charge, as many times as you like.

You may not:

  * **Take the artwork out.** The plates, sprite sheets and atlases may not be
    extracted, converted, modified, redistributed on their own, or reused in
    any other work, product, game or dataset, without written permission.

A fork of the source code is welcome under the licence in the first section.
**A fork must strip or replace `lib/art/` and `lib/tiles/`.** The game is built
to survive that: it draws a large glyph wherever a plate is missing, and tile
mode falls back to glyphs wherever optional artwork is absent.

How the artwork was made, stated plainly because it is better said than
discovered: the source images behind the character-art plates were generated
with AI image tools and converted to plates by this project's own code, which
measures each glyph's ink in the current typeface and pools the source pixels
against that ramp. The optional 32/64-pixel map sprites are deterministic
reductions of retained original portraits, using foreground-only colour sampling
and transparent padding. Wall and vegetation source images are shared with
the Ammerow project and reduced into separate scenery sheets.
Supplemental scenery and everyday-item sprites use original AI-generated
source sheets; generic category icons also reuse retained item illustrations.
No Ammerow monster identities or gameplay rules are imported. Original images and
sprite sheets are excluded from public source; conversion tools and synthetic
tests are included. Earlier experimental tile artwork remains subject to these
same separate artwork terms.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Sound effects and music
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The optional WAV files in `lib/xtra/sound/pack/` and
`lib/xtra/music/pack/` are copyright (c) 2026 John Horton, to the extent
copyright and related rights subsist. The effects are shared with Ammerow:
Lands Beyond; the title music is Ormeq - Home Theme (Dark).

They are supplied with official playable releases, separately from the
program's source terms. Normal play, personal backups, private modifications
and gameplay coverage, including monetised videos and streams, are permitted.
Asset redistribution, repackaging or reuse requires written permission except
where applicable law permits otherwise. Public source forks must omit or
replace these assets. Missing effects use Ormeq's original synth; missing
music stays silent. The public mapping, inventory, tests and playback code
remain under the program's source terms.

Full asset terms and production description: `licenses/Ormeq-Audio.txt`.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Game content
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The monsters, objects, quests, prose and place names in `lib/edit/` are
substantially rewritten from what was inherited, to remove material belonging
to other authors.

Where the data files, source headers, changelogs and help pages still say
"FrogComposband", that is deliberate and factual: a version stamp recording
which upstream release last edited a page, an attribution, or an answer to a
question about lineage. `lib/file/credits.txt` is upstream's own attribution
and is left exactly as it was written.

Artwork and audio are covered separately -- see the sections above.


